From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:45:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] library: panorama grids pick tall or wide columns from
 committed cover shapes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Each panorama grid votes its own mode from covers that have already
committed a shape. committedRatio returns 9/16 for an unknown id, so that
value is not a vote; committedRatioOrNull skips it. Wide is the existing
0.75 band.

A sample is trusted once the known count reaches min(total, max(8,
total / 2)). Below that the previous mode stays, including Unknown. The
first trusted sample is Wide at or above 0.60 and Tall below that. Wide
returns to Tall only at or below 0.40. The sample runs when the grid
settles, after the cross-band flush, and again if the listed count
changes while settled. A put does not recompute the mode and does not
bump PanoramaMasonryContentEpoch. The mode is read in composition, so the
content lambda identity changes and the layout cache rebuilds the spans.

Tall uses Shaped(1.5). Wide uses Shaped(2/3) and keeps every cover in one
lane, which is what stops a landscape shelf from leaving the right column
empty. Unknown stays on the width-only tier and still spans a landscape
cover when there is room. A fixed column count stays fixed; the span still
follows the mode.

Library comfortable and compact, and browse comfortable and compact, each
keep the mode in their own rememberSaveable. A category page is its own
composition, so a category change recounts.

与 anikku-harmony 0039 同源。
